# One ADR carrying rules in four categories projects one entry per rule into
# four populated sections, ordered by the configured vocabulary (not by rule
# order in the file), each citing the same carrying ADR (v0.2 D5/A1).

env CONSTITUTION_TODAY=2026-07-02

exec constitution adr new --title 'House rules' --body-file body.md
stdout 'created .*ADR-0001-house-rules\.md'

cmp constitution/constitution.md want-constitution.md

-- constitution.yml --
schemaVersion: 1
phase: sealed
consent:
  policy: off
sourceTracking:
  type: none
categories:
  - architecture
  - code-style
  - testing
  - process

-- body.md --
## Context and Problem Statement

x

## Considered Options

- a

## Decision Outcome

Adopt the house rules.

## Rules

### process

#### trunk-based
Commit to trunk behind feature flags.

### architecture

#### hex-core
Structure services as hexagonal.

### testing

#### three-tiers
Test in three tiers.

### code-style

#### gofmt-all
Format all Go code with gofmt.

-- want-constitution.md --
<!--
  GENERATED FILE -- projection of the ADR log in constitution/adr/.
  Do not hand-edit; changes will be overwritten by the next "constitution
  regen". Only the rules (## Rules entries) of active ADRs project here; to
  change a rule, add, supersede, or deprecate an ADR instead.
-->

# Constitution

The source of truth for this project's standing technical decisions — how
recurring problems are solved (architecture, mapping, testing, process) — so
that requirements can stay functional and need not re-explain implementation
choices.

Decision log: constitution/adr/.

## architecture

### hex-core

Structure services as hexagonal.

